        <history>
          <p>The Wind Quintet was written for the Copenhagen Wind Quintet after Nielsen heard the ensemble rehearsing Mozart and was struck by the distinct personality of each player. He is said to have set out to portray each musician's character through their instrument's music, giving the piece an unusually personal, almost theatrical quality among works for the medium.</p>
